  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "You can get an automatic six-month extension to file your federal income tax return, moving the deadline from April 15 to October 15, by filing Form 4868 by the April 15 deadline. This extension is only for submitting paperwork; any taxes owed must still be paid by April 15 to avoid penalties.How to File a Tax ExtensionIRS Free File: Use free tax software to electronically file Form 4868, regardless of your income.Pay Electronically: Make a payment via IRS Direct Pay, debit/credit card, or Digital Wallet and select \"Extension\" as the payment type. You will receive a confirmation number and do not need to file Form 4868.Mail Form 4868: Complete Form 4868 and mail it to the IRS postmarked by April 15.Important ConsiderationsNot an Extension to Pay: The extension only gives you more time to submit your return. You must estimate and pay your tax liability by April 15 to avoid interest and late payment penalties.Failure-to-File Penalty: Filing an extension prevents the 5% penalty (of unpaid taxes) per month for not filing, which can reach up to 25%.Disaster Relief: Taxpayers in specific disaster areas may be granted longer extensions automatically.Military/Foreign: Individuals stationed outside the U.S. or in combat zones may have specific, longer deadlines.",
